\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Retaining a path in the vacuum law}
\date{2026-11-11}

\p{A [coarse path map](fdip-00MO) records the ordered transport
 along selected chains of fine links. In the
 [vacuum process](fdip-00N9), each time slice is distributed
 by #{\Omega^2\nu}; even before a path is discarded, this
 differs from the independent Haar reference used to define
 the link Hilbert space. How does the actual image of this
 vacuum law determine an isometric comparison of fine and
 retained states, and when can its time evolution be generated
 by one retained Hamiltonian?}
